## 🤖 How to use AI agents most effectively as a beginner

**The loop that works:**

```
1. Copy the error message from your terminal
2. Paste it here (Claude) or into Jules
3. Say: "I got this error. Here is my current code: [paste code]"
4. Replace your file with the fixed version
5. Repeat
```

**Best prompts to use with Jules or Claude:**

| Situation | Prompt to use |
|---|---|
| Starting a file | *"Write a complete [filename] file for a FastAPI backend that [does X]. I am a beginner."* |
| Got an error | *"I got this error: [paste error]. My code is: [paste code]. Fix it."* |
| Something isn't working | *"My backend returns [X] but I expected [Y]. Here's my code: [paste]. What's wrong?"* |
| Need to understand something | *"Explain what this line does like I'm 15: [paste line]"* |

---These two are especially useful for your situation — Claude Code lets you point at your actual project folder and say "fix this error" or "add memory to my agent" and it edits your files directly. Much faster than copy-pasting back and forth.

